thub.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/deployments","created_at":"2014-06-12T16:00:38Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T22:36:14Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-12T23:00:16Z","git_url":"git://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:bazelbuild/bazel.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel","homepage":"https://bazel.build","size":992874,"stargazers_count":24886,"watchers_count":24886,"language":"Java","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":4359,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1819,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["bazel","build","build-system","correct","fast","multi-language","scalable","test"],"visibility":"public","forks":4359,"open_issues":1819,"watchers":24886,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Description of the feature request:\n\n\nGoogletest can produce structured output, in [XML](http://google.github.io/googletest/advanced.html#generating-an-xml-report) or [JSON](http://google.github.io/googletest/advanced.html#generating-a-json-report) format, via the `--gtest_output` option.  However, the resulting file isn't a declared output artifact, so it gets deleted along with the sandbox.\r\n\r\nThis was noticed in #757, which was fixed soon thereafter, but the linked commit 39125b2213d60a52db0a186e2887d007010221cd does not make it clear how to _use_ this feature.  (It also looks to my eye to be an XML-only solution.  We should find a solution that can handle JSON output as well.)\r\n\r\nCurrently, I can get the file by doing `bazel build`, and then running the binary via `./bazel-bin/path/to/my/binary`.  This is unsatisfactory because it doesn't scale: I'd like to be able to run `bazel test --test_arg=\"--gtest_output=json\" //package/...:all`, or something like that, and get a collection of JSON files whose paths, relative to some output root, mimic the package/target hierarchy of the test targets in `//package/...:all`.\r\n\r\nI am able to retain the sandbox information by running with `--sandbox_debug`, and I can _find_ the sandbox _location_ by running also with `--verbose_explanations`.  This is unsatisfactory for several reasons.  First, I need to read the output manually, as a human, and pattern-match to find the sandbox: I don't think a script would be able to do this _robustly_.  Second, each separate test target has its own sandbox (naturally), so I would need to visit a lot of different folder hierarchies to aggregate them all.\r\n\r\nIt seems like it would be nice to be able to declare the JSON report as an \"official\" output of the test rule.  Especially if we could generate a unique filename for each test target.  This would be easy to do with some bazel macro that wraps `cc_test`: we could generate the `name` from the input name, and provide the appropriate `--gtest_output` flag value under the hood.  However, `cc_test` has no `outs` parameter, so I don't know how to declare a new output for a `cc_test` rule.  Also, the discussion in #757 makes me think it's hard to have an \"optional\" output file, which might not be there sometimes.\r\n\r\nbazel and googletest are two great projects.  And the structured output googletest produces has tons of potential.  Let's fix the pipeline problem and help these projects play more nicely together!  :slightly_smiling_face: \n\n### What underlying problem are you trying to solve with this feature?\n\n\nI want an external system to parse the googletest structured output from a variety of targets, and generate custom reports for our internal purposes.  The fields included by default in the structured output are already useful.  I'm also easily able to augment them with extra fields according to the googletest documentation.\r\n\r\nTo meet my needs, I should be able to run via `bazel test`, so that I can run any desired subset of tests in parallel.  I also want the output JSON files to be found in a single hierarchy, with the complete pathname for each mirroring the package/target which generated it.  It would also be very helpful if the root of that hierarchy could be predictable.\n\n### Which operating system are you running Bazel on?\n\n\nUbuntu 18.04\n\n### What is the output of `bazel info release`?\n\n\nrelease 5.3.1\n\n### If `bazel info release` returns `development version` or `(@non-git)`, tell us how you built Bazel.\n\n\nN/A\n\n### What's the output of `git remote get-url origin; git rev-parse master; git rev-parse HEAD` ?\n\n\n```text\nIt's a proprietary, internal repo.  I suspect this information won't help this issue, but if I'm wrong, I'll seek permission to share.\n```\n\n\n### Have you found anything relevant by searching the web?\n\nhttps://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/commit/39125b2213d60a52db0a186e2887d007010221cd\r\nhttps://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/commit/36d2363f5a9cfd95c96c1af5303de2380e57d14e\n\n### Any other information, logs, or outputs that you want to share?\n\n_No response_","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/16507/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/16507/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]